# autorhythm: an SGS chip rhythm, which is where the EDGE RULE shows itself. On these
# masks the trigger is the rising edge of a ROM bit, so a mark whose predecessor is
# also marked is already sounding and cannot fire again; the panel says "edge-trig"
# and those cells are drawn HOLLOW. Machine 2 (]] from the FR-2L), then walk to a
# rhythm with adjacent marks: M252 AA rhythm 3 has them on two lanes.
tap 20 ]
tap 30 ]
tap 45 RIGHT
tap 55 RIGHT
tap 70 SPACE
